    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.which_mutual - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.which_mutual.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.which_mutual()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find pairs of mutual (reciprocal) edges in directed graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.which_mutual()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find pairs of mutual (reciprocal) edges in directed graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.which_mutual()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find pairs of mutual (reciprocal) edges in directed graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind pairs of mutual (reciprocal) edges in directed graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L88694-L88762){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.which_mutual()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Which mutual](../assets/graphs/which-mutual.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The shared graph, directed, with edge ids on every edge. A and B are joined both ways by edges 1 and 6, and C and D by edges 5 and 7, all in the accent color; the other edges are one-way. The card returns the mutual edge id pairs (1, 6) and (5, 7).\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nIdentifies edge pairs where both A->B and B->A exist, indicating bidirectional\nconnections. Only meaningful for directed graphs. Each pair is returned once\nwith edge IDs in ascending order.\n\nThis is useful for analyzing reciprocity patterns in social networks,\ncommunication graphs, and other directed relationships.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[tuple[int, int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   List of (edge_id1, edge_id2) tuples representing mutual edge pairs.\n    Empty list if no mutual edges exist.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If called on an undirected graph.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~reciprocity`) \n\n:   The share of edges that run both ways.\n\n[](`~count_mutual_node_pairs`) \n\n:   Count the pairs of nodes joined both ways.\n\n[](`~which_multiple`) \n\n:   Find parallel edges instead.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nAna and Ben follow each other, so their two edges form a mutual pair, while the edge to\nCruz has no partner:\n\n::: {#53b59b42 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"Ana\", \"Ben\"), (\"Ben\", \"Ana\"), (\"Ana\", \"Cruz\")], directed=True\n)\n\ngraph.which_mutual()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[(1, 2)]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Paying each other back\n\n`payments()` is a month of payments between 18 accounts at a made-up bank, each directed\nfrom payer to payee. Only two pairs of accounts pay each other. The flatmates Max and Nia\nsplit the rent: Nia pays Max 900, half of the 1,800 that Max pays the Landlord:\n\n::: {#4523f2c5 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport polars as pl\n\npayments = ec.payments()\nmutual = [e for pair in payments.which_mutual() for e in pair]\n\n(\n    payments.get_edge_df(labels=True)\n    .filter(pl.col(\"id\").is_in(mutual))\n    .select(\"source\", \"target\", \"amount\", \"date\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 4)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>source</th><th>target</th><th>amount</th><th>date</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>i64</td><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Dee&quot;</td><td>&quot;Eve&quot;</td><td>80</td><td>&quot;2026-03-02&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Nia&quot;</td><td>&quot;Max&quot;</td><td>900</td><td>&quot;2026-03-02&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Eve&quot;</td><td>&quot;Dee&quot;</td><td>25</td><td>&quot;2026-03-03&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Max&quot;</td><td>&quot;Nia&quot;</td><td>40</td><td>&quot;2026-03-08&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#b92de4b4 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.plot(highlight_edges=mutual, label_by=\"label\", seed=11)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57